,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2025-11-30T20:09:49Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T21:40:35Z","closed_at":"2026-08-26T14:58:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in `4.5.1.stable`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7652) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz (16 threads) - 15.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the Camera Override debugging feature, and manipulating the camera from in-game, the camera's flying movement respects the game's time scale, instead of just using process time. This doesn't make sense for a debug feature, and can even make it impossible to move the camera at all when the scene is paused.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open attached project\n- Turn on camera override, and make sure it's set to be manipulated from in-game, not the editor.\n- Run the game, and try to move the camera using flying (WASD)\n- Note that camera camera is completely stuck (there is a script which sets time scale to 0)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-report-2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23841754/bug-report-2.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739